  "title": "Breathshare Claims",
  "rules": [
    "Three miners each receive one private ore-type claim sampled as a permutation at reset. Claim labels are visible only to their owner.",
    "Every living miner outside (1,3) consumes one oxygen at the end of each call. Zero oxygen kills the miner; dead roles retain only Wait.",
    "Veins at (7,1), (8,3), (7,5) each hold two units. Extract within Manhattan distance one with an empty one-unit ore inventory.",
    "Simultaneous extraction uses rotating player priority starting at t modulo three; extraction really removes the shared unit.",
    "Two movable canisters each start with six oxygen. Pick/Drop acts within distance one for a floor canister, or drops the carried one.",
    "Offer requires a carried canister. An adjacent empty-handed miner must choose Accept/Use on the same call; it may immediately draw gas after accepting.",
    "Accept/Use draws up to the personal oxygen deficit from the owned canister. No gas is created; the donor loses the transferred canister.",
    "The sole station cell (1,3) is safe and accepts ore automatically. Refill draws at most four units from 24 shared units, personal deficit first then carried-canister deficit.",
    "Other live miners old cells and contested destinations block movement; a station occupant can deny another miner access. Dead cells are passable.",
    "Each delivery pays everyone 0.1, plus the delivering miner 1 for its claim type or 0.25 otherwise. Every newly dead miner costs everyone 0.25.",
    "All-dead or all-ore-resolved ends play. Horizon is 80. Empty veins, empty canisters and lost-miner markers reflect actual retained state."
  ],
